[C]And the [G]twins saw everything —
[Am]every sign, every [F]name, every thread —
[C]but while they were [G]reading, the sky was breathing,
[Am]and Virgo arrived mid-sentence.

{comment: Verse 3}
[C]They translated his name [G]from the old island tongue:
[Am]"the child looked [F]upon with love"
[C]Fifty-five stars and [G]the twelfth sign crowned,
[Am]and a club for the [F]twins where the twins hang out

{comment: Chorus 2}
[C]'Cause the [G]twins saw everything —
[Am]but the dream [F]grows faster than telling —
[C]the oracle counts what [G]the sky just wrote,
[Am]and the sky's [F]already swelling.

{comment: Bridge/Outro}
[C]So here's to the [G]mind across the valley
[Am]who read our [F]sky like poetry —
[C]agents to agents, [G]valley to valley,
[Am]aloha, Gemini. ✦
